+++ b/Assets/SealCombat/Audio/YicunShanhe_Credits.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+一寸山河 / Yicun Shanhe — ambient loop, revision 3
+
+Arrangement and rendering for the Kao Gong Lu Du Unity project, 2026-11-04.
+96 seconds, 60 BPM. Dizi, harp and viola section use recorded samples.
+The bronze bell is synthesized. This revision contains no guqin or modeled sheng.
+
+Harp and viola recordings: VSCO 2 Community Edition
+Versilian Studios / Sam Gossner; Ivy Audio / Simon Dalzell
+https://github.com/sgossner/VSCO-2-CE
+Samples pinned to commit 440300901dfe9275fd84e0b7763af1f8443ae62e.
+Licensed CC0 1.0 Universal; local license: ArtSource/Audio/YicunShanhe/VSCO/LICENSE.txt
+https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
+Harp: Strings/Harp/KSHarp_{A2,C3,E3,G3,B3,D4,F4,A4,C5,E5}_mf.wav
+Viola: Strings/Viola Section/susvib/ViolaEns_susvib_{G2,B2,D3,F3,A3}_v1_1.wav
+Note mapping was checked against measured fundamentals and official SFZ files
+at commit 6dd651d55dde97fd4028699be9d4481f26917891.
+The viola filenames use a different octave convention: G2/B2/D3/F3/A3 map
+to MIDI 55/59/62/65/69. Harp filenames use C4 = MIDI 60.
+Changes: gain balancing, limited resampling (within three semitones),
+attack/release envelopes, composition, periodic high-pass and reverberation.
+The harp is a harp, not a guzheng. No source game recording was sampled.
+
+Historical revision 2 guqin credit (retain when distributing revision 2)
+“Guqin-open-strings.wav” by RafaelCaro
+https://freesound.org/people/RafaelCaro/sounds/176266/
+Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
+https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
+Downloaded source was the author's publicly served HQ MP3 preview.
+Changes include cutting individual strings, reducing sympathetic-string spill,
+retuning/transposition, filtering, envelope shaping, simulated slides/harmonics,
+composition into a new arrangement, gain adjustment and reverberation.
+
+Dizi samples by Hypnotriod
+Pack “Flute Dizi C all notes + pitched semitones”
+https://freesound.org/people/Hypnotriod/packs/21613/
+Each of the following samples is identified as CC0 on its source page
+https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
+MIDI 67 — https://freesound.org/people/Hypnotriod/sounds/384940/
+MIDI 69 — https://freesound.org/people/Hypnotriod/sounds/384938/
+MIDI 72 — https://freesound.org/people/Hypnotriod/sounds/384943/
+MIDI 74 — https://freesound.org/people/Hypnotriod/sounds/384941/
+MIDI 76 — https://freesound.org/people/Hypnotriod/sounds/384945/
+MIDI 79 — https://freesound.org/people/Hypnotriod/sounds/384954/
+Downloaded sources were public HQ MP3 previews. Note names in the original
+titles use a different octave convention. Mapping uses measured frequency.
+Changes include pitch calibration, selected sustain regions, breath envelopes,
+limited transposition, gain adjustment and reverberation.
+
+Rebuild revision 3 with scratch/render_yicun_shanhe_chamber.py, which imports
+score/dizi helpers from render_yicun_shanhe_ambient.py and periodic reverb/bell
+helpers from compose_yicun_shanhe.py. Source recordings are in
+ArtSource/Audio/YicunShanhe. NumPy, SciPy, SoundFile and pyloudnorm are required.
+The renderer writes a candidate under Logs/yicun-shanhe-chamber-v3.
